<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Basel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1431–1449</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of Basel was a general council of the Catholic Church that met at Basel from 1431, continuing the conciliar movement. It made peace with the moderate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussites">Hussites</a> but clashed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-eugene-iv">Pope Eugene IV</a>, who moved the council to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> in 1437; the members who stayed deposed him and elected the antipope Felix V, a former Duke of Savoy. It dissolved in 1449.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-basel.jpg" alt="Council of Basel" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michel Wolgemut, Wilhelm Pleydenwurff (Hartmann Schedel, editor) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuremberg_chronicles_f_244v_2_Concilium_florentinum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
